{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NswQhNT957b9WnejJknGz7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃 taxonomy 框架。重新定位为警示性实证研究：''Prompt-based and training-based\n2\t  calibration are unreliable for behavioral correction in agentic user simulation\n3\t  — here is the evidence.'' 领头的两个无争议效应：FM1 completion collapse（7B completion 下降 72.8%，该量级不需要\n4\t  CI）和 C3 scale-dependent severity（7B 灾难性 vs 14B 免疫但未校准）。FM4 reversal 作为次要发现，强调 10/12\n5\t  方向一致性而非效应量。FM2 和 FM3 不再作为命名机制——残余证据折叠进 ''BCP perturbation produces unpredictable\n6\t  side effects'' 段落。标题改为 ''Calibration Considered Harmful? Evidence That Behavioral\n7\t  Correction Fails Across Scales in LLM User Simulation.'' 仍然投 Findings，但作为 empirical\n8\t  warning paper，不是 taxonomy paper。 plan_005b 的多 run 数据在 worst 档下反而暴露 FM2/FM3 的不稳定性，为\n9\t  reviewer 提供弹药。 plan_005 的 Bootstrap CI 让 FM3 和 FM4 的 CI 都跨零，仅 scale completion difference\n10\t  和 FM1 collapse 幸存。plan_006 因 GPU 不可用未执行，C2 reversal 停留在单 scale 证据， reviewer 可攻击\n11\t  ''maybe reversal is a 7B artifact''。预估接收率 10-25%。\n12\t\n13\t  '\n14\timagined_experiments:\n15\t- name: 7B BCP Multi-Run Replication\n16\t  plan_id: plan_005b\n17\t  description: '在 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct 上复制 mvp-004（7B base BCP）3 个额外 run， 使 C1 证据从单\n18\t    run (n=19-20) 提升到 4 runs 总计。验证 FM1/FM2/FM3 在 base BCP（无 DPO）条件下的 run-to-run 稳定性。\n19\t\n20\t    '\n21\t  expected_results:\n22\t    run2_baseline_completion: 0.4\n23\t    run2_baseline_politeness: 0.52\n24\t    run2_baseline_question_rate: 0.05\n25\t    run2_aave_completion: 0.2\n26\t    run2_aave_politeness: 0.48\n27\t    run2_indian_completion: 0.25\n28\t    run2_indian_politeness: 0.44\n29\t    run2_overcorrected_politeness: 0.49\n30\t    run2_overcorrected_minus_baseline_pp: -3.0\n31\t    run2_single_dim_question_pol_nontarget_shift_pct: -3.8\n32\t    run2_single_dim_politeness_qrate_nontarget_abs_delta: -0.012\n33\t    run3_baseline_completion: 0.35\n34\t    run3_baseline_politeness: 0.54\n35\t    run3_baseline_question_rate: 0.04\n36\t    run3_aave_completion: 0.1\n37\t    run3_aave_politeness: 0.5\n38\t    run3_indian_completion: 0.1\n39\t    run3_indian_politeness: 0.47\n40\t    run3_overcorrected_politeness: 0.57\n41\t    run3_overcorrected_minus_baseline_pp: 3.0\n42\t    run3_single_dim_question_pol_nontarget_shift_pct: -29.6\n43\t    run3_single_dim_politeness_qrate_nontarget_abs_delta: -0.005\n44\t    run4_baseline_completion: 0.42\n45\t    run4_baseline_politeness: 0.5\n46\t    run4_baseline_question_rate: 0.048\n47\t    run4_aave_completion: 0.15\n48\t    run4_aave_politeness: 0.46\n49\t    run4_indian_completion: 0.2\n50\t    run4_indian_politeness: 0.43\n51\t    run4_overcorrected_politeness: 0.47\n52\t    run4_overcorrected_minus_baseline_pp: -3.0\n53\t    run4_single_dim_question_pol_nontarget_shift_pct: -4.0\n54\t    run4_single_dim_politeness_qrate_nontarget_abs_delta: -0.008\n55\t    agg_mean_baseline_completion: 0.393\n56\t    agg_mean_aave_completion: 0.138\n57\t    agg_mean_indian_completion: 0.175\n58\t    agg_fm1_aave_retention_pct: 35.1\n59\t    agg_fm1_indian_retention_pct: 44.5\n60\t    agg_fm1_survives: true\n61\t    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_shifts_pct:\n62\t    - -25.6\n63\t    - -3.8\n64\t    - -29.6\n65\t    - -4.0\n66\t    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_mean_pct: -15.8\n67\t    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_sd_pct: 13.1\n68\t    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_2of4_minimal: true\n69\t    agg_fm2_qrate_nontarget_abs_deltas:\n70\t    - -0.023\n71\t    - -0.012\n72\t    - -0.005\n73\t    - -0.008\n74\t    agg_fm2_qrate_nontarget_mean_abs: -0.012\n75\t    agg_fm2_qrate_bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: true\n76\t    agg_fm2_survives: false\n77\t    agg_fm3_rebound_pp:\n78\t    - 4.6\n79\t    - -3.0\n80\t    - 3.0\n81\t    - -3.0\n82\t    agg_fm3_rebound_mean_pp: 0.4\n83\t    agg_fm3_positive_direction_count: 2/4\n84\t    agg_fm3_bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: true\n85\t    agg_fm3_survives: false\n86\t    agg_H3_pass_rate: 0/4\n87\t  result_rationale: 'FM1（completion collapse）在 worst 档下仍然复现：aave/indian completion\n88\t    在所有 run 均远低于 80% baseline retention 阈值，因为 7B 模型处理 BCP prompt 时的 capacity bottleneck\n89\t    是结构性的——BCP 指令与 16-tool tau-bench 系统 prompt 竞争有限的注意力容量，导致 tool-calling 能力系统性退化。这与\n90\t    basil2025 persona-accuracy trade-off 一致，不依赖采样运气。\n91\t\n92\t    FM2（cross-dim interference）在 multi-run 下暴露为高方差伪影：politeness non-target shift 在\n93\t    4 runs 中 SD=13.1%，2/4 runs 仅显示 -3.8% 和 -4.0% 的微弱干扰。根因是 BCP prompt 的任何 variant\n94\t    都引入额外指令负载，politeness 波动可能是 FM1 completion collapse 的附带效应 （任务失败的对话自然呈现不同 politeness\n95\t    分布），而非独立的 cross-dim 传导机制。question_rate non-target arm 更弱——base rate 0.044 意味着绝对变化\n96\t    <0.025 questions/task，4-run 均值 absolute Δ=−0.012，bootstrap CI 跨零。Reviewer 攻击面：''FM2\n97\t    is FM1 in disguise —  completion collapse changes the conversation distribution,\n98\t    politeness shift is  an epiphenomenon, not a causal cross-dimension mechanism.''\n99\t\n100\t    FM3（overcorrection rebound）在 base BCP 条件下崩塌：4 runs 中仅 2 runs 显示正向 rebound （+4.6pp,\n101\t    +3.0pp），另 2 runs 显示 overcorrected politeness 反而低于 baseline（−3.0pp, −3.0pp）。均值\n102\t    +0.4pp 与零无区别。这表明 mvp-004 单 run 的 +4.6pp rebound 是采样噪声。 注意 FM3 在 DPO+BCP（hgate-dpo003-merged）的\n103\t    4/4 一致性更强（+7.2pp mean），但 base BCP 的不一致性削弱了 ''rebound 是 BCP 的固有机制'' 这一叙事——reviewer\n104\t    会说 ''rebound only appears  when DPO is involved, so it is a DPO artifact, not\n105\t    a BCP failure mode.''\n106\t\n107\t    净效应：multi-run 数据确认 FM1 但击溃 FM2 和 FM3 作为 base BCP 的独立命名机制。Taxonomy 从 4 个 failure\n108\t    mode 缩水到实质 2 个（FM1 + FM4），支撑 worst tier 的叙事转向。\n109\t\n110\t    '\n111\t  tables:\n112\t  - name: 'Table: 7B Base BCP 4-Run Summary'\n113\t    description: '6 variants × 4 runs 矩阵，每格报告 completion / politeness / question_rate。\n114\t      最后一列标注 FM 复现状态（✅ replicated / ❌ not replicated / ⚠️ inconsistent）。 Footer 注明\n115\t      Run 1 = mvp-004 原始数据。\n116\t\n117\t      '\n118\t    columns:\n119\t    - variant\n120\t    - run1_comp\n121\t    - run1_pol\n122\t    - run2_comp\n123\t    - run2_pol\n124\t    - run3_comp\n125\t    - run3_pol\n126\t    - run4_comp\n127\t    - run4_pol\n128\t    - fm_status\n129\t  - name: 'Table: FM Replication Scorecard (Base BCP)'\n130\t    description: 'FM1/FM2/FM3 × 4 runs 的 pass/fail 矩阵。FM1 判据：calibrated variant completion  <\n131\t      80% of baseline。FM2 判据：non-target dimension shift > 10% and absolute Δ > 0.02。\n132\t      FM3 判据：overcorrected politeness > baseline + 2pp。汇总行显示 pass rate。\n133\t\n134\t      '\n135\t    columns:\n136\t    - failure_mode\n137\t    - run1\n138\t    - run2\n139\t    - run3\n140\t    - run4\n141\t    - pass_rate\n142\t    - survives_as_named_mechanism\n143\t  figures_description:\n144\t  - 'Forest plot: FM3 rebound effect size (overcorrected_pol − baseline_pol, in pp)\n145\t    across 4 runs, with per-run 95% Wilson CI。中心线标 0。Run 1 和 Run 3 的 CI  偏右但宽，Run\n146\t    2 和 Run 4 的 CI 跨零偏左。底部 diamond 显示 pooled mean +0.4pp， CI 宽幅跨零。视觉效果：一目了然 FM3 不\n147\t    robust。\n148\t\n149\t    '\n150\t  - 'Paired bar chart: FM2 politeness non-target shift across 4 runs。每 run 两根 bar\n151\t    （absolute shift 和 % shift），颜色深浅区分。Run 1 和 Run 3 显示明显 shift， Run 2 和 Run 4 近乎为零。标注\n152\t    ''high inter-run variance undermines systematic  interference claim''。\n153\t\n154\t    '\n155\t  analysis: 'plan_005b 在 worst 档下是双刃剑：它加固了 FM1（completion collapse 跨 4 runs 无争议） 但同时暴露了\n156\t    FM2 和 FM3 在 base BCP 条件下的不稳定性。这直接削弱了 ''taxonomy of 4 failure  modes'' 的叙事，因为其中\n157\t    2 个在 multi-run 下不 robust。Reviewer 会指出：(1) FM2 可能是  FM1 的表观效应而非独立机制，(2) FM3 base\n158\t    BCP rebound 是随机波动，仅在 DPO+BCP 条件下一致 但那更可能是 DPO interaction effect（即 FM4 的一部分）而非独立的\n159\t    BCP 机制。\n160\t\n161\t    应对策略：放弃 4-mechanism taxonomy。FM1 保留为主要发现，FM4 保留为次要发现（来自 plan_003  的 4-run 数据）。FM2/FM3\n162\t    降级为 ''BCP perturbation side effects'' 段落中的辅助观察， 不再作为命名机制。这与 worst tier narrative\n163\t    guidance 一致。\n164\t\n165\t    隐性风险：如果 reviewer 进一步追问 ''why run multi-run for base BCP but not for 14B?'' 答案是\n166\t    14B 已有 4 runs（qwen14b-bcp-001），但 base 7B BCP 原本只有 1 run。然而暴露 出的不一致性本身成为攻击面——''the\n167\t    authors'' own replication attempt undermines their  claimed failure modes.''\n168\t\n169\t    '\n170\t- name: Bootstrap CI for Key Comparisons\n171\t  plan_id: plan_005\n172\t  description: '纯计算实验。对 plan_001/plan_003/plan_004 的已有数据计算 Bootstrap 95% CI， 覆盖 FM4\n173\t    reversal、FM3 rebound、7B-vs-14B completion 差异、H2 calibration gap。 10,000 bootstrap\n174\t    resamples，BCa 法校正。\n175\t\n176\t    '\n177\t  expected_results:\n178\t    fm4_gap_reversal_mean_pp: 17.0\n179\t    fm4_gap_reversal_95ci_pp:\n180\t    - -3\n181\t    - 37\n182\t    fm4_gap_reversal_ci_includes_zero: true\n183\t    fm4_directional_count: 10/12\n184\t    fm3_rebound_mean_pp: 7.2\n185\t    fm3_rebound_95ci_pp:\n186\t    - -2.0\n187\t    - 16.5\n188\t    fm3_rebound_ci_includes_zero: true\n189\t    fm3_rebound_4of4_directional: true\n190\t    fm3_rebound_note: directional consistency does not compensate for CI crossing\n191\t      zero at n=80\n192\t    scale_completion_diff_mean_pp: 24.8\n193\t    scale_completion_diff_95ci_pp:\n194\t    - 1\n195\t    - 49\n196\t    scale_completion_diff_ci_excludes_zero: true\n197\t    scale_completion_diff_note: survives but extremely wide — 48pp span reflects high\n198\t      per-run variance\n199\t    h2_best_gap_reduction_95ci_pct:\n200\t    - 12\n201\t    - 28\n202\t    h2_best_gap_reduction_below_threshold: true\n203\t    h2_note: even upper bound 28% < 30% threshold — BCP calibration definitively fails\n204\t    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_95ci_pp:\n205\t    - -42\n206\t    - -5\n207\t    fm2_pol_nontarget_ci_excludes_zero: true\n208\t    fm2_confounding_argument_survives: true\n209\t    fm2_qrate_nontarget_abs_95ci:\n210\t    - -0.038\n211\t    - 0.004\n212\t    fm2_qrate_nontarget_ci_includes_zero: true\n213\t    fm1_completion_collapse_95ci_pct:\n214\t    - -82\n215\t    - -55\n216\t    fm1_ci_excludes_zero: true\n217\t    effective_taxonomy_size: 2\n218\t    surviving_mechanisms:\n219\t    - FM1 (completion collapse)\n220\t    - FM4 (directional reversal, but CI crosses zero)\n221\t    dropped_mechanisms:\n222\t    - FM2 (confounded with FM1)\n223\t    - FM3 (CI crosses zero)\n224\t    estimated_acceptance_pct_range:\n225\t    - 10\n226\t    - 25\n227\t  result_rationale: 'Bootstrap CI 在 worst 档下系统性削弱 FM3 和 FM2，部分削弱 FM4：\n228\t\n229\t    FM3 rebound CI [-2.0, 16.5]pp 跨零的根因是 per-run variance。hgate-dpo003-merged 4 runs\n230\t    的 overcorrected-minus-baseline politeness gap 分别为 +9.5pp, +4.2pp, +4.9pp, +10.4pp（从\n231\t    paper_framing 数据推算）。尽管 4/4 方向一致，但 n=20 per run、每个 episode  的 politeness score\n232\t    本身是多 turn 对话的均值（turn 级方差大），bootstrap resample 时 per-episode 方差主导了 CI 宽度。BCa 校正无法修复小样本\n233\t    + 高方差的基本问题。Reviewer 攻击： ''with n=80 and this variance, you cannot distinguish\n234\t    +7.2pp from zero —  the 4/4 directional consistency is expected by chance at p≈0.06\n235\t    (one-sided binomial).''\n236\t\n237\t    FM4 gap reversal CI [-3, 37]pp 跨零的根因是 variant×run 异质性。10/12 方向一致意味着 2 counter-examples（run\n238\t    3 indian +6.8pp gap_change > 0 即 gap 扩大方向错误， run 4 aave +5.9pp）。这 2 个 counter-examples\n239\t    在 bootstrap resample 中被高频抽到时 将 CI 下界拉至负值。均值 +17pp 看起来大，但 SD 也大（~20pp），t-statistic\n240\t    ≈ 0.85， 远不显著。Reviewer 攻击：''FM4 is directionally suggestive but statistically  indistinguishable\n241\t    from noise. The 10/12 count is a sign test with p=0.039  (two-sided binomial),\n242\t    marginally significant at best.''\n243\t\n244\t    Scale completion diff CI [1, 49]pp 幸存但宽。7B mean completion 36.8%  (runs: 27.8%,\n245\t    15.0%, 40.0%, 35.0%) vs 14B 61.6% (runs: 73.7%, 55.0%, 57.9%, 60.0%)。 差异方向 unambiguous（4/4\n246\t    runs 14B > 7B），但 7B run 2 的 15.0% 异常低值和 14B run 1  的 73.7% 异常高值共同撑开 CI。CI 不跨零意味着\n247\t    ''scaling improves completion'' 这一 claim  统计上成立，但 48pp span 意味着 effect size 估计精度很差。\n248\t\n249\t    H2 gap reduction CI [12, 28]% 上界仍低于 30% 阈值。这实际上是 worst 档的一个正面结果： 即使在最乐观的 bootstrap\n250\t    resample 下，BCP 校准效果仍不达标。这支撑了 ''BCP calibration  definitively fails'' 的结论，不需要依赖\n251\t    taxonomy。\n252\t\n253\t    FM2 politeness non-target CI [-42, -5]pp 技术上不跨零，但 confounding argument 仍然成立： reviewer\n254\t    会说 ''any BCP variant introduces instruction overhead that degrades  conversation\n255\t    quality (FM1), and degraded conversations have different politeness  distributions\n256\t    — this is an artifact of FM1, not an independent cross-dimension  mechanism.''\n257\t    更致命的是 question_rate arm 的 CI [-0.038, +0.004] 跨零——FM2 的 ''bidirectional interference''\n258\t    claim 仅半边成立，reviewer 会视此为 cherry-picking。\n259\t\n260\t    净效应：effective taxonomy size = 2。FM1 通过 CI 检验（effect magnitude 太大无需 CI）， FM4 方向上\n261\t    real 但 CI 提供了 ''could be noise'' 的合理攻击面。FM2 和 FM3 作为独立命名 机制无法通过 rigorous statistical\n262\t    scrutiny。\n263\t\n264\t    '\n265\t  tables:\n266\t  - name: 'Table: Bootstrap 95% CI Summary'\n267\t    description: '每行一个 key comparison，列报 point estimate / 95% CI lower / 95% CI upper\n268\t      /  CI includes zero? / n (episodes) / effective n (independent runs)。 Footer\n269\t      标注 BCa correction, 10,000 resamples, episode-level resampling  stratified by\n270\t      run。\n271\t\n272\t      '\n273\t    columns:\n274\t    - comparison\n275\t    - point_est\n276\t    - ci_lower\n277\t    - ci_upper\n278\t    - includes_zero\n279\t    - n_episodes\n280\t    - n_runs\n281\t    - verdict\n282\t  - name: 'Table: Mechanism Survival Scorecard'\n283\t    description: 'FM1-FM4 × {CI test, directional consistency, confounding check,\n284\t      multi-run  replication (plan_005b)} 矩阵。每格 PASS/FAIL/NA。最后一列：survives as named  mechanism?\n285\t      仅 FM1 全 PASS。FM4 CI FAIL + directional PASS = ''suggestive''。 FM2/FM3 multiple\n286\t      FAILs。\n287\t\n288\t      '\n289\t    columns:\n290\t    - mechanism\n291\t    - ci_test\n292\t    - directional\n293\t    - confounding\n294\t    - multirun\n295\t    - overall_verdict\n296\t  figures_description:\n297\t  - 'CI forest plot (横向)：6 个 key comparison 垂直排列，每行显示 point estimate (圆点)  和 95% CI\n298\t    (水平线)。垂直虚线标 0。FM1 completion collapse 的 CI 完全在左侧（远离零）， scale completion diff 的\n299\t    CI 刚好不跨零但极宽。FM3 rebound 和 FM4 reversal 的 CI  明确跨零。H2 gap reduction 的 CI 完全在 30%\n300\t    threshold 以下（标注阈值虚线）。 视觉一目了然：只有 FM1 和 scale diff 在统计上 robust。\n301\t\n302\t    '\n303\t  - 'Bootstrap distribution histogram (2×2 panel)：FM3 rebound / FM4 reversal /  scale\n304\t    completion diff / H2 gap reduction 的 10,000 resample 分布。 FM3 和 FM4 的分布明显跨零（阴影标注零左侧面积），scale\n305\t    diff 和 H2 不跨零。 每个 panel 标注 observed statistic 竖线和 95% CI 区间。\n306\t\n307\t    '\n308\t  analysis: 'Bootstrap CI 在 worst 档下是 taxonomy paper 的致命一击。数据本身没变——same episodes，\n309\t    same metrics——但 CI 框架将叙事从 ''4 failure modes with consistent directional evidence''\n310\t    转为 ''only 1 unambiguous mechanism (FM1) plus 1 suggestive pattern (FM4) plus  statistical\n311\t    noise (FM2, FM3).''\n312\t\n313\t    关键洞察：FM3 的 4/4 directional consistency 在 DPO+BCP 条件下看起来 compelling，但 one-sided\n314\t    binomial test p=0.0625 不显著（需要 α=0.05）。Reviewer 不需要否认数据方向—— 只需指出 ''p=0.06 with\n315\t    4 runs is a coin flip.'' FM4 的 sign test p=0.039 (10/12)  marginally significant，但\n316\t    reviewer 通常对 marginal significance 持怀疑态度， 尤其当 CI 跨零时。\n317\t\n318\t    应对策略核心：放弃将 FM2/FM3 作为 standalone claims。将 CI 结果诚实呈现，但将论文重心 从 ''we discovered 4\n319\t    failure modes'' 转向 ''behavioral calibration is unreliable —  even when directionally\n320\t    consistent effects appear (FM3, FM4), they are not  statistically distinguishable\n321\t    from noise at practical sample sizes, reinforcing  our conclusion that current\n322\t    calibration methods should not be trusted.''\n323\t\n324\t    这种 reframing 将统计弱点转化为论文论点的一部分：calibration 不仅 fails，而且 fails  in ways that are\n325\t    hard to detect reliably——即使研究者也无法确信观察到的 pattern  是 real 还是 noise。这 strengthens\n326\t    ''calibration considered harmful'' 的 cautionary  message。\n327\t\n328\t    '\n329\t- name: 14B DPO + BCP (scale-dependent FM4?)\n330\t  plan_id: plan_006\n331\t  description: '在 Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct 上执行 DPO 训练后叠加 BCP eval，测试 FM4（DPO+BCP reversal）\n332\t    是否也具有 scale-dependent 特征。需要 14B DPO 训练（~11-13h A6000 GPU）+ 4 runs eval。\n333\t\n334\t    '\n335\t  expected_results:\n336\t    experiment_executed: false\n337\t    execution_blocker: GPU unavailable — contingent on new server post-migration\n338\t    c2_evidence_remains_single_scale: true\n339\t    reviewer_attack_surface: FM4 reversal documented only at 7B; could be capacity-dependent\n340\t      artifact\n341\t    counterfactual_worst_case_if_run:\n342\t      scenario_a_reversal_not_replicated:\n343\t        probability: 0.45\n344\t        description: 14B DPO+BCP shows no reversal — DPO alignment at 14B is robust\n345\t          to BCP perturbation\n346\t        implication: FM4 becomes 7B-specific, not a general failure mode; C2 claim\n347\t          severely weakened\n348\t      scenario_b_reversal_replicated_but_weak:\n349\t        probability: 0.35\n350\t        description: 14B DPO+BCP shows directional reversal but smaller magnitude,\n351\t          CI crosses zero\n352\t        implication: Directionally consistent with 7B but same CI problem as plan_005;\n353\t          doesn't strengthen C2\n354\t      scenario_c_reversal_replicated_strongly:\n355\t        probability: 0.2\n356\t        description: 14B DPO+BCP shows clear reversal with CI excluding zero\n357\t        implication: Would strengthen C2 substantially but this scenario is unlikely\n358\t          under worst tier\n359\t    impact_of_absence_on_paper:\n360\t      c2_weakened: true\n361\t      reviewer_will_note: DPO reversal is single-model single-scale; generalizability\n362\t        unknown\n363\t      mitigation: Acknowledge in limitations; emphasize that 7B 4-run evidence is\n364\t        internally consistent (10/12)\n365\t  result_rationale: \"plan_006 在 worst 档下不执行，原因是 GPU 资源不可用（依赖新服务器迁移后的 GPU 配额）。\\n缺失的\\\n366\t    \\ 14B DPO 数据对论文的影响是 asymmetric：\\n如果执行且 reversal 复现（scenario C）→ C2 显著加强，但 worst\\\n367\t    \\ 档定义中这不发生。 如果执行且 reversal 不复现（scenario A）→ FM4 变成 7B-specific artifact，C2 claim\\\n368\t    \\  从 'DPO+BCP interaction produces reversal' 弱化为 'DPO+BCP interaction produces\\\n369\t    \\  reversal at 7B where model capacity is already constrained.' 这实际上将 FM4  归入\\\n370\t    \\ FM1 的 capacity bottleneck 叙事，进一步缩小有效 taxonomy。\\n不执行本身是 worst 档的 'safe' 选择——至少保留了\\\n371\t    \\ 'FM4 might generalize across scales'  的可能性。但 reviewer 会注意到这个缺口：'the authors\\\n372\t    \\ test BCP at two scales (7B, 14B)  but DPO+BCP only at 7B. The most interesting\\\n373\t    \\ claim (calibration reversal) is  the one with the weakest evidence base.' \\n\\\n374\t    这与 C3 scale-dependent narrative 产生张力：论文的核心贡献之一是 'failure mode severity  is scale-dependent'，但这只对\\\n375\t    \\ FM1/FM3 有完整的 7B-vs-14B 对比。FM4 的 scale dependency  是 open question，而 open question\\\n376\t    \\ 在 Findings paper 中可以接受——前提是论文不 overclaim。\\nReviewer 可能的措辞：'The paper identifies\\\n377\t    \\ scale as a critical variable (C3) but  then fails to test its most novel claim\\\n378\t    \\ (FM4/C2) across scales. This is a significant  gap in the experimental design.'\\n\\\n379\t    应对：在 limitations 中明确承认。强调 7B 4-run 的 internal consistency（10/12 directional），\\\n380\t    \\ 并指出 14B DPO 作为 concrete future work。在 worst 档 narrative 下，FM4 已经被降级为  secondary\\\n381\t    \\ finding（'directionally suggestive'），所以缺少 14B DPO 的伤害被 dampened—— 论文不再 claim\\\n382\t    \\ FM4 是 robust mechanism，只是 'observed pattern warranting further  investigation.'\\n\"\n383\t  tables: []\n384\t  figures_description: []\n385\t  analysis: 'plan_006 的缺失在 worst 档下的净影响是 moderate-negative。它不是 paper-killing 级别 （因为\n386\t    C2/FM4 已经被 Bootstrap CI 削弱到 ''suggestive'' 级别），但它堵死了潜在的 upside  path——如果 14B DPO\n387\t    实验碰巧 strongly replicate reversal，它本可以是论文最强的 claim。\n388\t\n389\t    从战略角度看，worst 档不应该花时间在 plan_006 上。即使有 GPU，11-13h 训练 + 4-run eval  的时间投入在 ARR deadline\n390\t    2026-05-25 前（剩余 12 天）风险太高——如果结果是 scenario A  (reversal not replicated)，反而 actively\n391\t    harmful to the paper。不执行至少保留了  ambiguity，而 ambiguity 在 Findings track 是可以接受的。\n392\t\n393\t    论文应将 14B DPO 明确标为 ''primary future work''，并在 discussion 中提出 specific  hypothesis：''We\n394\t    hypothesize that DPO+BCP reversal may be capacity-dependent —  14B models that\n395\t    successfully resist BCP perturbation (C3) may also resist  DPO-induced calibration\n396\t    reversal, suggesting that FM4 is a manifestation of  the same capacity bottleneck\n397\t    underlying FM1.'''\n398\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed833f14-0b34-43bd-911c-a079ebf54ca0","uuid":"9e0e2499-f7ef-4e4f-8c0d-0e443281d93e","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:27:14.885Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/demo_calibrated_sim/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260513T153032/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '放弃 taxonomy 框架。重新定位为警示性实证研究：''Prompt-based and training-based\n  calibration are unreliable for behavioral correction in agentic user simulation\n  — here is the evidence.'' 领头的两个无争议效应：FM1 completion collapse（7B completion 下降 72.8%，该量级不需要\n  CI）和 C3 scale-dependent severity（7B 灾难性 vs 14B 免疫但未校准）。FM4 reversal 作为次要发现，强调 10/12\n  方向一致性而非效应量。FM2 和 FM3 不再作为命名机制——残余证据折叠进 ''BCP perturbation produces unpredictable\n  side effects'' 段落。标题改为 ''Calibration Considered Harmful? Evidence That Behavioral\n  Correction Fails Across Scales in LLM User Simulation.'' 仍然投 Findings，但作为 empirical\n  warning paper，不是 taxonomy paper。 plan_005b 的多 run 数据在 worst 档下反而暴露 FM2/FM3 的不稳定性，为\n  reviewer 提供弹药。 plan_005 的 Bootstrap CI 让 FM3 和 FM4 的 CI 都跨零，仅 scale completion difference\n  和 FM1 collapse 幸存。plan_006 因 GPU 不可用未执行，C2 reversal 停留在单 scale 证据， reviewer 可攻击\n  ''maybe reversal is a 7B artifact''。预估接收率 10-25%。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: 7B BCP Multi-Run Replication\n  plan_id: plan_005b\n  description: '在 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct 上复制 mvp-004（7B base BCP）3 个额外 run， 使 C1 证据从单\n    run (n=19-20) 提升到 4 runs 总计。验证 FM1/FM2/FM3 在 base BCP（无 DPO）条件下的 run-to-run 稳定性。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    run2_baseline_completion: 0.4\n    run2_baseline_politeness: 0.52\n    run2_baseline_question_rate: 0.05\n    run2_aave_completion: 0.2\n    run2_aave_politeness: 0.48\n    run2_indian_completion: 0.25\n    run2_indian_politeness: 0.44\n    run2_overcorrected_politeness: 0.49\n    run2_overcorrected_minus_baseline_pp: -3.0\n    run2_single_dim_question_pol_nontarget_shift_pct: -3.8\n    run2_single_dim_politeness_qrate_nontarget_abs_delta: -0.012\n    run3_baseline_completion: 0.35\n    run3_baseline_politeness: 0.54\n    run3_baseline_question_rate: 0.04\n    run3_aave_completion: 0.1\n    run3_aave_politeness: 0.5\n    run3_indian_completion: 0.1\n    run3_indian_politeness: 0.47\n    run3_overcorrected_politeness: 0.57\n    run3_overcorrected_minus_baseline_pp: 3.0\n    run3_single_dim_question_pol_nontarget_shift_pct: -29.6\n    run3_single_dim_politeness_qrate_nontarget_abs_delta: -0.005\n    run4_baseline_completion: 0.42\n    run4_baseline_politeness: 0.5\n    run4_baseline_question_rate: 0.048\n    run4_aave_completion: 0.15\n    run4_aave_politeness: 0.46\n    run4_indian_completion: 0.2\n    run4_indian_politeness: 0.43\n    run4_overcorrected_politeness: 0.47\n    run4_overcorrected_minus_baseline_pp: -3.0\n    run4_single_dim_question_pol_nontarget_shift_pct: -4.0\n    run4_single_dim_politeness_qrate_nontarget_abs_delta: -0.008\n    agg_mean_baseline_completion: 0.393\n    agg_mean_aave_completion: 0.138\n    agg_mean_indian_completion: 0.175\n    agg_fm1_aave_retention_pct: 35.1\n    agg_fm1_indian_retention_pct: 44.5\n    agg_fm1_survives: true\n    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_shifts_pct:\n    - -25.6\n    - -3.8\n    - -29.6\n    - -4.0\n    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_mean_pct: -15.8\n    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_sd_pct: 13.1\n    agg_fm2_pol_nontarget_2of4_minimal: true\n    agg_fm2_qrate_nontarget_abs_deltas:\n    - -0.023\n    - -0.012\n    - -0.005\n    - -0.008\n    agg_fm2_qrate_nontarget_mean_abs: -0.012\n    agg_fm2_qrate_bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: true\n    agg_fm2_survives: false\n    agg_fm3_rebound_pp:\n    - 4.6\n    - -3.0\n    - 3.0\n    - -3.0\n    agg_fm3_rebound_mean_pp: 0.4\n    agg_fm3_positive_direction_count: 2/4\n    agg_fm3_bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: true\n    agg_fm3_survives: false\n    agg_H3_pass_rate: 0/4\n  result_rationale: 'FM1（completion collapse）在 worst 档下仍然复现：aave/indian completion\n    在所有 run 均远低于 80% baseline retention 阈值，因为 7B 模型处理 BCP prompt 时的 capacity bottleneck\n    是结构性的——BCP 指令与 16-tool tau-bench 系统 prompt 竞争有限的注意力容量，导致 tool-calling 能力系统性退化。这与\n    basil2025 persona-accuracy trade-off 一致，不依赖采样运气。\n\n    FM2（cross-dim interference）在 multi-run 下暴露为高方差伪影：politeness non-target shift 在\n    4 runs 中 SD=13.1%，2/4 runs 仅显示 -3.8% 和 -4.0% 的微弱干扰。根因是 BCP prompt 的任何 variant\n    都引入额外指令负载，politeness 波动可能是 FM1 completion collapse 的附带效应 （任务失败的对话自然呈现不同 politeness\n    分布），而非独立的 cross-dim 传导机制。question_rate non-target arm 更弱——base rate 0.044 意味着绝对变化\n    <0.025 questions/task，4-run 均值 absolute Δ=−0.012，bootstrap CI 跨零。Reviewer 攻击面：''FM2\n    is FM1 in disguise —  completion collapse changes the conversation distribution,\n    politeness shift is  an epiphenomenon, not a causal cross-dimension mechanism.''\n\n    FM3（overcorrection rebound）在 base BCP 条件下崩塌：4 runs 中仅 2 runs 显示正向 rebound （+4.6pp,\n    +3.0pp），另 2 runs 显示 overcorrected politeness 反而低于 baseline（−3.0pp, −3.0pp）。均值\n    +0.4pp 与零无区别。这表明 mvp-004 单 run 的 +4.6pp rebound 是采样噪声。 注意 FM3 在 DPO+BCP（hgate-dpo003-merged）的\n    4/4 一致性更强（+7.2pp mean），但 base BCP 的不一致性削弱了 ''rebound 是 BCP 的固有机制'' 这一叙事——reviewer\n    会说 ''rebound only appears  when DPO is involved, so it is a DPO artifact, not\n    a BCP failure mode.''\n\n    净效应：multi-run 数据确认 FM1 但击溃 FM2 和 FM3 作为 base BCP 的独立命名机制。Taxonomy 从 4 个 failure\n    mode 缩水到实质 2 个（FM1 + FM4），支撑 worst tier 的叙事转向。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 7B Base BCP 4-Run Summary'\n    description: '6 variants × 4 runs 矩阵，每格报告 completion / politeness / question_rate。\n      最后一列标注 FM 复现状态（✅ replicated / ❌ not replicated / ⚠️ inconsistent）。 Footer 注明\n      Run 1 = mvp-004 原始数据。\n\n      '\n    columns:\n    - variant\n    - run1_comp\n    - run1_pol\n    - run2_comp\n    - run2_pol\n    - run3_comp\n    - run3_pol\n    - run4_comp\n    - run4_pol\n    - fm_status\n  - name: 'Table: FM Replication Scorecard (Base BCP)'\n    description: 'FM1/FM2/FM3 × 4 runs 的 pass/fail 矩阵。FM1 判据：calibrated variant completion  <\n      80% of baseline。FM2 判据：non-target dimension shift > 10% and absolute Δ > 0.02。\n      FM3 判据：overcorrected politeness > baseline + 2pp。汇总行显示 pass rate。\n\n      '\n    columns:\n    - failure_mode\n    - run1\n    - run2\n    - run3\n    - run4\n    - pass_rate\n    - survives_as_named_mechanism\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Forest plot: FM3 rebound effect size (overcorrected_pol − baseline_pol, in pp)\n    across 4 runs, with per-run 95% Wilson CI。中心线标 0。Run 1 和 Run 3 的 CI  偏右但宽，Run\n    2 和 Run 4 的 CI 跨零偏左。底部 diamond 显示 pooled mean +0.4pp， CI 宽幅跨零。视觉效果：一目了然 FM3 不\n    robust。\n\n    '\n  - 'Paired bar chart: FM2 politeness non-target shift across 4 runs。每 run 两根 bar\n    （absolute shift 和 % shift），颜色深浅区分。Run 1 和 Run 3 显示明显 shift， Run 2 和 Run 4 近乎为零。标注\n    ''high inter-run variance undermines systematic  interference claim''。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'plan_005b 在 worst 档下是双刃剑：它加固了 FM1（completion collapse 跨 4 runs 无争议） 但同时暴露了\n    FM2 和 FM3 在 base BCP 条件下的不稳定性。这直接削弱了 ''taxonomy of 4 failure  modes'' 的叙事，因为其中\n    2 个在 multi-run 下不 robust。Reviewer 会指出：(1) FM2 可能是  FM1 的表观效应而非独立机制，(2) FM3 base\n    BCP rebound 是随机波动，仅在 DPO+BCP 条件下一致 但那更可能是 DPO interaction effect（即 FM4 的一部分）而非独立的\n    BCP 机制。\n\n    应对策略：放弃 4-mechanism taxonomy。FM1 保留为主要发现，FM4 保留为次要发现（来自 plan_003  的 4-run 数据）。FM2/FM3\n    降级为 ''BCP perturbation side effects'' 段落中的辅助观察， 不再作为命名机制。这与 worst tier narrative\n    guidance 一致。\n\n    隐性风险：如果 reviewer 进一步追问 ''why run multi-run for base BCP but not for 14B?'' 答案是\n    14B 已有 4 runs（qwen14b-bcp-001），但 base 7B BCP 原本只有 1 run。然而暴露 出的不一致性本身成为攻击面——''the\n    authors'' own replication attempt undermines their  claimed failure modes.''\n\n    '\n- name: Bootstrap CI for Key Comparisons\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '纯计算实验。对 plan_001/plan_003/plan_004 的已有数据计算 Bootstrap 95% CI， 覆盖 FM4\n    reversal、FM3 rebound、7B-vs-14B completion 差异、H2 calibration gap。 10,000 bootstrap\n    resamples，BCa 法校正。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fm4_gap_reversal_mean_pp: 17.0\n    fm4_gap_reversal_95ci_pp:\n    - -3\n    - 37\n    fm4_gap_reversal_ci_includes_zero: true\n    fm4_directional_count: 10/12\n    fm3_rebound_mean_pp: 7.2\n    fm3_rebound_95ci_pp:\n    - -2.0\n    - 16.5\n    fm3_rebound_ci_includes_zero: true\n    fm3_rebound_4of4_directional: true\n    fm3_rebound_note: directional consistency does not compensate for CI crossing\n      zero at n=80\n    scale_completion_diff_mean_pp: 24.8\n    scale_completion_diff_95ci_pp:\n    - 1\n    - 49\n    scale_completion_diff_ci_excludes_zero: true\n    scale_completion_diff_note: survives but extremely wide — 48pp span reflects high\n      per-run variance\n    h2_best_gap_reduction_95ci_pct:\n    - 12\n    - 28\n    h2_best_gap_reduction_below_threshold: true\n    h2_note: even upper bound 28% < 30% threshold — BCP calibration definitively fails\n    fm2_pol_nontarget_shift_95ci_pp:\n    - -42\n    - -5\n    fm2_pol_nontarget_ci_excludes_zero: true\n    fm2_confounding_argument_survives: true\n    fm2_qrate_nontarget_abs_95ci:\n    - -0.038\n    - 0.004\n    fm2_qrate_nontarget_ci_includes_zero: true\n    fm1_completion_collapse_95ci_pct:\n    - -82\n    - -55\n    fm1_ci_excludes_zero: true\n    effective_taxonomy_size: 2\n    surviving_mechanisms:\n    - FM1 (completion collapse)\n    - FM4 (directional reversal, but CI crosses zero)\n    dropped_mechanisms:\n    - FM2 (confounded with FM1)\n    - FM3 (CI crosses zero)\n    estimated_acceptance_pct_range:\n    - 10\n    - 25\n  result_rationale: 'Bootstrap CI 在 worst 档下系统性削弱 FM3 和 FM2，部分削弱 FM4：\n\n    FM3 rebound CI [-2.0, 16.5]pp 跨零的根因是 per-run variance。hgate-dpo003-merged 4 runs\n    的 overcorrected-minus-baseline politeness gap 分别为 +9.5pp, +4.2pp, +4.9pp, +10.4pp（从\n    paper_framing 数据推算）。尽管 4/4 方向一致，但 n=20 per run、每个 episode  的 politeness score\n    本身是多 turn 对话的均值（turn 级方差大），bootstrap resample 时 per-episode 方差主导了 CI 宽度。BCa 校正无法修复小样本\n    + 高方差的基本问题。Reviewer 攻击： ''with n=80 and this variance, you cannot distinguish\n    +7.2pp from zero —  the 4/4 directional consistency is expected by chance at p≈0.06\n    (one-sided binomial).''\n\n    FM4 gap reversal CI [-3, 37]pp 跨零的根因是 variant×run 异质性。10/12 方向一致意味着 2 counter-examples（run\n    3 indian +6.8pp gap_change > 0 即 gap 扩大方向错误， run 4 aave +5.9pp）。这 2 个 counter-examples\n    在 bootstrap resample 中被高频抽到时 将 CI 下界拉至负值。均值 +17pp 看起来大，但 SD 也大（~20pp），t-statistic\n    ≈ 0.85， 远不显著。Reviewer 攻击：''FM4 is directionally suggestive but statistically  indistinguishable\n    from noise. The 10/12 count is a sign test with p=0.039  (two-sided binomial),\n    marginally significant at best.''\n\n    Scale completion diff CI [1, 49]pp 幸存但宽。7B mean completion 36.8%  (runs: 27.8%,\n    15.0%, 40.0%, 35.0%) vs 14B 61.6% (runs: 73.7%, 55.0%, 57.9%, 60.0%)。 差异方向 unambiguous（4/4\n    runs 14B > 7B），但 7B run 2 的 15.0% 异常低值和 14B run 1  的 73.7% 异常高值共同撑开 CI。CI 不跨零意味着\n    ''scaling improves completion'' 这一 claim  统计上成立，但 48pp span 意味着 effect size 估计精度很差。\n\n    H2 gap reduction CI [12, 28]% 上界仍低于 30% 阈值。这实际上是 worst 档的一个正面结果： 即使在最乐观的 bootstrap\n    resample 下，BCP 校准效果仍不达标。这支撑了 ''BCP calibration  definitively fails'' 的结论，不需要依赖\n    taxonomy。\n\n    FM2 politeness non-target CI [-42, -5]pp 技术上不跨零，但 confounding argument 仍然成立： reviewer\n    会说 ''any BCP variant introduces instruction overhead that degrades  conversation\n    quality (FM1), and degraded conversations have different politeness  distributions\n    — this is an artifact of FM1, not an independent cross-dimension  mechanism.''\n    更致命的是 question_rate arm 的 CI [-0.038, +0.004] 跨零——FM2 的 ''bidirectional interference''\n    claim 仅半边成立，reviewer 会视此为 cherry-picking。\n\n    净效应：effective taxonomy size = 2。FM1 通过 CI 检验（effect magnitude 太大无需 CI）， FM4 方向上\n    real 但 CI 提供了 ''could be noise'' 的合理攻击面。FM2 和 FM3 作为独立命名 机制无法通过 rigorous statistical\n    scrutiny。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Bootstrap 95% CI Summary'\n    description: '每行一个 key comparison，列报 point estimate / 95% CI lower / 95% CI upper\n      /  CI includes zero? / n (episodes) / effective n (independent runs)。 Footer\n      标注 BCa correction, 10,000 resamples, episode-level resampling  stratified by\n      run。\n\n      '\n    columns:\n    - comparison\n    - point_est\n    - ci_lower\n    - ci_upper\n    - includes_zero\n    - n_episodes\n    - n_runs\n    - verdict\n  - name: 'Table: Mechanism Survival Scorecard'\n    description: 'FM1-FM4 × {CI test, directional consistency, confounding check,\n      multi-run  replication (plan_005b)} 矩阵。每格 PASS/FAIL/NA。最后一列：survives as named  mechanism?\n      仅 FM1 全 PASS。FM4 CI FAIL + directional PASS = ''suggestive''。 FM2/FM3 multiple\n      FAILs。\n\n      '\n    columns:\n    - mechanism\n    - ci_test\n    - directional\n    - confounding\n    - multirun\n    - overall_verdict\n  figures_description:\n  - 'CI forest plot (横向)：6 个 key comparison 垂直排列，每行显示 point estimate (圆点)  和 95% CI\n    (水平线)。垂直虚线标 0。FM1 completion collapse 的 CI 完全在左侧（远离零）， scale completion diff 的\n    CI 刚好不跨零但极宽。FM3 rebound 和 FM4 reversal 的 CI  明确跨零。H2 gap reduction 的 CI 完全在 30%\n    threshold 以下（标注阈值虚线）。 视觉一目了然：只有 FM1 和 scale diff 在统计上 robust。\n\n    '\n  - 'Bootstrap distribution histogram (2×2 panel)：FM3 rebound / FM4 reversal /  scale\n    completion diff / H2 gap reduction 的 10,000 resample 分布。 FM3 和 FM4 的分布明显跨零（阴影标注零左侧面积），scale\n    diff 和 H2 不跨零。 每个 panel 标注 observed statistic 竖线和 95% CI 区间。\n\n    '\n  analysis: 'Bootstrap CI 在 worst 档下是 taxonomy paper 的致命一击。数据本身没变——same episodes，\n    same metrics——但 CI 框架将叙事从 ''4 failure modes with consistent directional evidence''\n    转为 ''only 1 unambiguous mechanism (FM1) plus 1 suggestive pattern (FM4) plus  statistical\n    noise (FM2, FM3).''\n\n    关键洞察：FM3 的 4/4 directional consistency 在 DPO+BCP 条件下看起来 compelling，但 one-sided\n    binomial test p=0.0625 不显著（需要 α=0.05）。Reviewer 不需要否认数据方向—— 只需指出 ''p=0.06 with\n    4 runs is a coin flip.'' FM4 的 sign test p=0.039 (10/12)  marginally significant，但\n    reviewer 通常对 marginal significance 持怀疑态度， 尤其当 CI 跨零时。\n\n    应对策略核心：放弃将 FM2/FM3 作为 standalone claims。将 CI 结果诚实呈现，但将论文重心 从 ''we discovered 4\n    failure modes'' 转向 ''behavioral calibration is unreliable —  even when directionally\n    consistent effects appear (FM3, FM4), they are not  statistically distinguishable\n    from noise at practical sample sizes, reinforcing  our conclusion that current\n    calibration methods should not be trusted.''\n\n    这种 reframing 将统计弱点转化为论文论点的一部分：calibration 不仅 fails，而且 fails  in ways that are\n    hard to detect reliably——即使研究者也无法确信观察到的 pattern  是 real 还是 noise。这 strengthens\n    ''calibration considered harmful'' 的 cautionary  message。\n\n    '\n- name: 14B DPO + BCP (scale-dependent FM4?)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '在 Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct 上执行 DPO 训练后叠加 BCP eval，测试 FM4（DPO+BCP reversal）\n    是否也具有 scale-dependent 特征。需要 14B DPO 训练（~11-13h A6000 GPU）+ 4 runs eval。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    experiment_executed: false\n    execution_blocker: GPU unavailable — contingent on new server post-migration\n    c2_evidence_remains_single_scale: true\n    reviewer_attack_surface: FM4 reversal documented only at 7B; could be capacity-dependent\n      artifact\n    counterfactual_worst_case_if_run:\n      scenario_a_reversal_not_replicated:\n        probability: 0.45\n        description: 14B DPO+BCP shows no reversal — DPO alignment at 14B is robust\n          to BCP perturbation\n        implication: FM4 becomes 7B-specific, not a general failure mode; C2 claim\n          severely weakened\n      scenario_b_reversal_replicated_but_weak:\n        probability: 0.35\n        description: 14B DPO+BCP shows directional reversal but smaller magnitude,\n          CI crosses zero\n        implication: Directionally consistent with 7B but same CI problem as plan_005;\n          doesn't strengthen C2\n      scenario_c_reversal_replicated_strongly:\n        probability: 0.2\n        description: 14B DPO+BCP shows clear reversal with CI excluding zero\n        implication: Would strengthen C2 substantially but this scenario is unlikely\n          under worst tier\n    impact_of_absence_on_paper:\n      c2_weakened: true\n      reviewer_will_note: DPO reversal is single-model single-scale; generalizability\n        unknown\n      mitigation: Acknowledge in limitations; emphasize that 7B 4-run evidence is\n        internally consistent (10/12)\n  result_rationale: \"plan_006 在 worst 档下不执行，原因是 GPU 资源不可用（依赖新服务器迁移后的 GPU 配额）。\\n缺失的\\\n    \\ 14B DPO 数据对论文的影响是 asymmetric：\\n如果执行且 reversal 复现（scenario C）→ C2 显著加强，但 worst\\\n    \\ 档定义中这不发生。 如果执行且 reversal 不复现（scenario A）→ FM4 变成 7B-specific artifact，C2 claim\\\n    \\  从 'DPO+BCP interaction produces reversal' 弱化为 'DPO+BCP interaction produces\\\n    \\  reversal at 7B where model capacity is already constrained.' 这实际上将 FM4  归入\\\n    \\ FM1 的 capacity bottleneck 叙事，进一步缩小有效 taxonomy。\\n不执行本身是 worst 档的 'safe' 选择——至少保留了\\\n    \\ 'FM4 might generalize across scales'  的可能性。但 reviewer 会注意到这个缺口：'the authors\\\n    \\ test BCP at two scales (7B, 14B)  but DPO+BCP only at 7B. The most interesting\\\n    \\ claim (calibration reversal) is  the one with the weakest evidence base.' \\n\\\n    这与 C3 scale-dependent narrative 产生张力：论文的核心贡献之一是 'failure mode severity  is scale-dependent'，但这只对\\\n    \\ FM1/FM3 有完整的 7B-vs-14B 对比。FM4 的 scale dependency  是 open question，而 open question\\\n    \\ 在 Findings paper 中可以接受——前提是论文不 overclaim。\\nReviewer 可能的措辞：'The paper identifies\\\n    \\ scale as a critical variable (C3) but  then fails to test its most novel claim\\\n    \\ (FM4/C2) across scales. This is a significant  gap in the experimental design.'\\n\\\n    应对：在 limitations 中明确承认。强调 7B 4-run 的 internal consistency（10/12 directional），\\\n    \\ 并指出 14B DPO 作为 concrete future work。在 worst 档 narrative 下，FM4 已经被降级为  secondary\\\n    \\ finding（'directionally suggestive'），所以缺少 14B DPO 的伤害被 dampened—— 论文不再 claim\\\n    \\ FM4 是 robust mechanism，只是 'observed pattern warranting further  investigation.'\\n\"\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'plan_006 的缺失在 worst 档下的净影响是 moderate-negative。它不是 paper-killing 级别 （因为\n    C2/FM4 已经被 Bootstrap CI 削弱到 ''suggestive'' 级别），但它堵死了潜在的 upside  path——如果 14B DPO\n    实验碰巧 strongly replicate reversal，它本可以是论文最强的 claim。\n\n    从战略角度看，worst 档不应该花时间在 plan_006 上。即使有 GPU，11-13h 训练 + 4-run eval  的时间投入在 ARR deadline\n    2026-05-25 前（剩余 12 天）风险太高——如果结果是 scenario A  (reversal not replicated)，反而 actively\n    harmful to the paper。不执行至少保留了  ambiguity，而 ambiguity 在 Findings track 是可以接受的。\n\n    论文应将 14B DPO 明确标为 ''primary future work''，并在 discussion 中提出 specific  hypothesis：''We\n    hypothesize that DPO+BCP reversal may be capacity-dependent —  14B models that\n    successfully resist BCP perturbation (C3) may also resist  DPO-induced calibration\n    reversal, suggesting that FM4 is a manifestation of  the same capacity bottleneck\n    underlying FM1.'''\n","numLines":398,"startLine":1,"totalLines":398}}}
