{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JsoUFaqQveK7ydv9VYbxMd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://www.ecnlpir.org/reviewerguidelines.html\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 and the review process, though the specific \"Findings reviewer guidelines review form\" document wasn't directly available in the results. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Process Overview\n\nSubmissions and reviews for EMNLP 2026 will be performed via the Open Review platform, with authors submitting to ACL Rolling Review (ARR) where they receive reviews and meta-reviews, then committing their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements and Timeline\n\nIf reviewers receive assignments, reviews must be completed by July 6, or meta-reviews by July 29.\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\n## Reviewer Qualifications\n\nReviewers are considered qualified if they have published at least two short or long papers in main ACL events or Findings, plus at least one more paper in the ACL Anthology or a major ML/AI venue.\n\nFor the specific EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official EMNLP 2026 website at https://2026.emnlp.org/ or the ARR platform at aclrollingreview.org, as these documents may be hosted there but weren't captured in my search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed833f14-0b34-43bd-911c-a079ebf54ca0","uuid":"325846d4-0076-4608-8c12-12dff21f0581","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:27:32.485Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FPV5xrYg95ThjDFmx4xfPr","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://www.ecnlpir.org/reviewerguidelines.html"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...","url":"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"Based on my search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 and the review process, though the specific \"Findings reviewer guidelines review form\" document wasn't directly available in the results. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Process Overview\n\nSubmissions and reviews for EMNLP 2026 will be performed via the Open Review platform, with authors submitting to ACL Rolling Review (ARR) where they receive reviews and meta-reviews, then committing their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements and Timeline\n\nIf reviewers receive assignments, reviews must be completed by July 6, or meta-reviews by July 29.\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\n## Reviewer Qualifications\n\nReviewers are considered qualified if they have published at least two short or long papers in main ACL events or Findings, plus at least one more paper in the ACL Anthology or a major ML/AI venue.\n\nFor the specific EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official EMNLP 2026 website at https://2026.emnlp.org/ or the ARR platform at aclrollingreview.org, as these documents may be hosted there but weren't captured in my search results."],"durationSeconds":6.236326818999998}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011dxZ2QPZQCCSmAHxFhsMsz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form ACL ARR\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Criteria for Determining Irresponsible Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer-policies/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025) – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"Surviving ARR May Meta-Review & Deciding on EMNLP 2025: A Tactical and Honest Guide | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/113/surviving-arr-may-meta-review-deciding-on-emnlp-2025-a-tactical-and-honest-guide\"},{\"title\":\"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and the ARR review system. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Review Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n## Review Form and Recommendations\n\nThe ARR review form includes several key components:\n\n- **Overall Assessment Scores**: The form includes options like \"Resubmit next cycle\" for papers needing substantial revisions completable by the next ARR cycle, \"Resubmit after next cycle\" for revisions requiring longer timelines, and \"Do not resubmit\" for papers that need to be fully redone or are not relevant to the ACL community.\n\n- **Reproducibility and Ethics Assessments**: Reviewers are asked whether authors have adequately discussed limitations and societal impacts, if there are ethical issues with the paper, and whether there is enough information for readers to reproduce results.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Policies\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nFor EMNLP 2025 specifically, the EMNLP 2025 PCs published initial criteria for 'highly irresponsible' reviewers, covering the non-submission of (meta-)reviews on time without due warning, extremely terse reviews for good-faith submissions, and egregious cases of unprofessional tone and LLM policy violations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed833f14-0b34-43bd-911c-a079ebf54ca0","uuid":"298edd28-0598-400e-a0a8-0a6572cb3fc4","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:27:34.372Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form ACL ARR","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DgKjd9BaGS3hkKL3Tnrq8N","content":[{"title":"Criteria for Determining Irresponsible Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer-policies/"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025) – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"Surviving ARR May Meta-Review & Deciding on EMNLP 2025: A Tactical and Honest Guide | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/113/surviving-arr-may-meta-review-deciding-on-emnlp-2025-a-tactical-and-honest-guide"},{"title":"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"}]},"I found relevant information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and the ARR review system. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Review Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n## Review Form and Recommendations\n\nThe ARR review form includes several key components:\n\n- **Overall Assessment Scores**: The form includes options like \"Resubmit next cycle\" for papers needing substantial revisions completable by the next ARR cycle, \"Resubmit after next cycle\" for revisions requiring longer timelines, and \"Do not resubmit\" for papers that need to be fully redone or are not relevant to the ACL community.\n\n- **Reproducibility and Ethics Assessments**: Reviewers are asked whether authors have adequately discussed limitations and societal impacts, if there are ethical issues with the paper, and whether there is enough information for readers to reproduce results.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Policies\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nFor EMNLP 2025 specifically, the EMNLP 2025 PCs published initial criteria for 'highly irresponsible' reviewers, covering the non-submission of (meta-)reviews on time without due warning, extremely terse reviews for good-faith submissions, and egregious cases of unprofessional tone and LLM policy violations."],"durationSeconds":7.528919901000001}}
