{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ft8JmUWrugSKcSimdt5ekD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 soundness excitement overall score scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Surviving ARR May Meta-Review & Deciding on EMNLP 2025: A Tactical and Honest Guide | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/113/surviving-arr-may-meta-review-deciding-on-emnlp-2025-a-tactical-and-honest-guide\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form and its scoring scales. Here are the key details:\n\n## Three-Score System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score Scale (1-5)\n\nThe soundness score evaluates whether the research is technically sound. The form asks whether the submission is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers considers the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. The scale includes:\n\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n## Excitement Score Scale (1-5)\n\nThe form asks \"How exciting is this paper for you?\" and notes that excitement is subjective, and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field. The scale includes:\n\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 1 = Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community (e.g. it is in no way related to computational processing of language).\n\n## Overall Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed833f14-0b34-43bd-911c-a079ebf54ca0","uuid":"4731060d-7d83-43cb-b87b-db0e12a93792","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:28:00.252Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 soundness excitement overall score scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01V7jKdbPLZkrZ8T372Zh9V8","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/acguidelines.md at main · yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/yoshitomo-matsubara/aclrollingreview/blob/main/acguidelines.md"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"},{"title":"Surviving ARR May Meta-Review & Deciding on EMNLP 2025: A Tactical and Honest Guide | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/113/surviving-arr-may-meta-review-deciding-on-emnlp-2025-a-tactical-and-honest-guide"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form and its scoring scales. Here are the key details:\n\n## Three-Score System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score Scale (1-5)\n\nThe soundness score evaluates whether the research is technically sound. The form asks whether the submission is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them, and for experimental papers considers the depth and/or breadth of research questions, technical soundness of experiments, and methodological validity of evaluation. The scale includes:\n\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n## Excitement Score Scale (1-5)\n\nThe form asks \"How exciting is this paper for you?\" and notes that excitement is subjective, and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field. The scale includes:\n\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 1 = Not Exciting: this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community (e.g. it is in no way related to computational processing of language).\n\n## Overall Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":8.612099423}}
