{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7EAkHsn3KWfrMpuCvpoXe","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment score scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Action Editor Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/actioneditorform\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/responsibleNLPresearch/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR SAC Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ARR review form and overall assessment score scale:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. \n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nFor the specific score scale on the review form, I found that the scale includes: 5 (The paper is largely complete and there are no clear points of revision), 4 (There are minor points that may be revised), 3 (There are major points that may be revised), 2 (The paper would need significant revisions to reach a publishable state), and 1 (Even after revisions, the paper is not likely to be publishable at an *ACL venue).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed833f14-0b34-43bd-911c-a079ebf54ca0","uuid":"42e2b29f-f279-4ed9-8c14-daa79e210c21","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:28:09.867Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform overall assessment score scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017AhrE8txsTE2BRypFmgk7L","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Response to ACL 2023 Questions","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Action Editor Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/actioneditorform"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/responsibleNLPresearch/"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR SAC Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ARR review form and overall assessment score scale:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. \n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\nFor the specific score scale on the review form, I found that the scale includes: 5 (The paper is largely complete and there are no clear points of revision), 4 (There are minor points that may be revised), 3 (There are major points that may be revised), 2 (The paper would need significant revisions to reach a publishable state), and 1 (Even after revisions, the paper is not likely to be publishable at an *ACL venue)."],"durationSeconds":5.5724720720000045}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01C8hspmNKCQnpfgqjKpiYTP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the ARR review form scoring scales:\n\n**Soundness (1-5):**\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n- 2 = Weak: Some of the claims are not well-supported.\n- 1 = Poor: The claims are not supported.\n\n\n- **Excitement (1-5):** ranges from Highly Exciting down to Not Exciting, capturing how novel or interesting the work is.\n- **Overall Assessment (1-5):** evaluates publication readiness, from papers needing no revision to those unlikely to be publishable even after significant work.\n\nNow I'm setting up a parallel review process where one reviewer focuses on the methods and experiments while another examines novelty and related work, then I'll guide them through a structured roundtable discussion moving from independent assessments to shared feedback and finally a converged synthesis.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":755,"cache_read_input_tokens":55766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":755},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed833f14-0b34-43bd-911c-a079ebf54ca0","uuid":"d9abb4a6-886b-4400-a621-83106df99733"}
