fference CI: [1, 49] pp.\n3. **FM4 (DPO-BCP interaction reversal, suggestive):** 10/12 directional consistency, sign test p=0.039, but magnitude CI [-3, +37] pp crosses zero.\n\n**Demoted observations:** FM2 (cross-dimension interference) and FM3 (overcorrection rebound) acknowledged as unreliable.\n\n**Related work cited:**\n- τ-bench [Yao et al., 2024] — benchmark for tool-calling agent evaluation\n- Sim2Real Gap Authors [2026] — sim-to-real gap in τ-bench\n- Seshadri et al. [2026] — AAVE and Indian English calibration issues\n- Basil et al. [2025] — persona prompting degrades MMLU accuracy (71.6% → 66.3%)\n- Hu et al. [2026] — expert persona degrades instruction-tuned models up to 30pp\n- Lee et al. [2024] — DPO bypasses rather than removes capabilities\n- Gupta et al. [2026] — bias spillover in targeted alignment\n- Rafailov et al. [2023] — DPO\n- Khan et al. [2026] — constrained decoding (mentioned in discussion)\n\n**Key narrative:** The paper frames itself as a \"cautionary empirical study\" rather than a taxonomy paper. The central conceptual contribution is the \"safety-efficacy gap\": scaling resolves BCP's destructive side effects without improving calibration effectiveness.\n\n**Limitations acknowledged:** Single model family (Qwen2.5 only), single task domain (τ-bench retail), small sample size (20 tasks per run), missing 14B DPO experiment, underpowered secondary findings.\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed R2 review focused on:\n\n1. **Novelty assessment:** How novel is the \"safety-efficacy gap\" concept? How novel is the finding that persona/calibration prompting degrades task performance? (Basil et al. 2025 and Hu et al. 2026 already documented this.) Is the extension to multi-turn tool-calling settings sufficiently novel?\n2. **Related work coverage:** Are there important missing references? Is the positioning relative to existing work accurate?\n3. **Contribution significance:** Is a negative result paper on a single model family and single domain sufficient for Findings? What is the actionable takeaway?\n4. **Framing and claims:** Is the title (\"Calibration Considered Harmful?\") appropriate given the evidence? Does the paper overclaim generalizability from Qwen2.5-only results?\n5. **Conceptual clarity:** Is the \"safety-efficacy gap\" concept well-defined and useful? Is the FM1-FM4 numbering appropriate given FM2/FM3 are demoted?\n6. **Missing perspectives:** Should the paper discuss other calibration approaches more thoroughly? Are there alternative explanations the paper misses?\n\nFormat your output as:\n\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty and Related Work\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, numbered W1, W2, etc.]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Bulleted list]\n\n### Detailed Comments\n[Section-by-section analysis]\n\n### Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Excitement: X/5\n- Overall: X/5\n\n### Confidence\n[1-5 scale: 5=absolutely certain, 4=quite sure, 3=fairly confident, 2=willing to be convinced, 1=guessing]\n```\n","uuid":"c632d836-26d9-4c27-bb1a-adbafaba4855","session_id":"ed833f14-0b34-43bd-911c-a079ebf54ca0"}
